  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Scope routing",
      "items": [
        "New features follow all seven Spec-Kit phases. Phase 7, Implement, is in View 2.",
        "Proposed clarification: fixes within approved scope link an existing task or finding. Changes to product behavior, schema, contracts or governing decisions return to the relevant Spec-Kit / ADR process."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Who participates",
      "items": [
        "Team Leader coordinates specification and tasks. Architect leads planning with affected domain agents. Use only the roles needed.",
        "Conflicting governing decisions pause dependent work for Karim; record accepted resolutions in the owning artifact."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "What reference means",
      "items": [
        "Attach the existing task ID or recorded bug/security finding to the change so its scope and completion can be traced. A task is planned work; a finding is a documented problem.",
        "This is an alternative route for a fix already inside approved scope, not a step after every new-feature approval. New scope follows the Spec-Kit path."
      ]
    }
  ]
